- op: discuss  # 5c37
  at: '2026-09-15T08:16:45Z'  # 5c37
  by: agent  # 5c37
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5c37
  clock: 4  # 5c37
  nonce: 5c37  # 5c37
  message: "SATISFIED by the dead-code walk entering the initializer. Behavioral evidence,\nlive repro, run before and after on the same input.\n\nREPRO (the item's own shape), hypergumbo self-analysis, 46,203 nodes:\n  hypergumbo dead-code-maybe --input .hypergumbo/self-analysis.json \\\n      --format json --cross-lang-threshold 0\n  BEFORE: 2,469 dead candidates, reachable_functions 2,755\n  AFTER:  2,448 dead candidates, reachable_functions 2,776\n  revived 21 = 18 __init__ + 3 downstream; newly dead 0; seed_count 1,266 both.\n\nCorpus, same command and flags:\n  pretix  13,907 -> 13,804  revived 103 (100 __init__ + 3 downstream), 0 newly dead\n  kserve     629 ->    555  revived  74 ( 69 __init__ + 5 downstream), 0 newly dead\n\nPREMISE RE-VERIFIED AT TIP, not taken from the item: of 11,428 instantiates\nedges, 9,217 land on kind=class, 2,211 on external_symbol, ZERO on a callable.\nAll 69 python X.__init__ methods have exactly one incoming edge type, contains.\n\nTHE ITEM'S SIZING CLAIM WAS WRONG AND IS NOW FILED. It recorded \"0 of 2,152\ndead candidates are __init__, so Python constructors are not currently\nmis-flagged\", and concluded the immediate win was ZERO. Reproduced (0 of\n2,252) -- but all 52 non-test __init__ ARE unreachable candidates. They are\nremoved by the cross-language demoter, which treats a substring hit in a\n.json/.yaml/.toml file as evidence of cross-language dispatch; __init__\nappears in pyproject.toml and five package YAMLs, clearing the threshold of 3\nin any Python repo. Filed as INV-hugit (masks 217 of 2,469 candidates, 8.8%,\nwith no disclosure bucket). So the harm was real and the instrument was hiding\nit, which is the opposite of the item's reading.\n\nTHE THREE DEFAULT-FLAG ROWS WERE READ BACK AGAINST SOURCE. All three are\nprivate helpers whose ONLY caller is the constructor: UnionFind.add,\nTrackerSet._load_last_list, and Cache._ensure_db -- which opens the tracker's\nSQLite connection and creates its schema. Deleting it breaks the cache.\n\nOPTION CHOSEN: none of A/B/C as written. Not A (re-point the dst):\nmethod_call_recovery keys its class hint on dst-in-class_ids, so re-pointing\npython would drop python from the linker that produced 89 edges here, for a\nmeasured gain of 3 rows. Not B (a linker minting edges): measured, it perturbs\ndetect_entrypoints and cost 5 route seeds on pretix (seed_count 1174 -> 1173),\nmaking 5 route symbols newly dead. The walk's OWN graph is augmented instead,\nafter seed detection -- no emitted edge moves, no other consumer moves, and\nthe resulting dead set is identical to the linker arm with zero newly dead.\n\nPrecision preserved: the hop needs (class is the dst of a construction edge)\nAND (member is its initializer). contains alone confers nothing, pinned by\nTestContainmentStillConfersNothing.\n\nRESIDUALS, filed not folded: INV-hugit (demoter), WI-rupot\n(method_call_recovery drops constructor-dst hints, latent since WI-fagit\nPR #689), WI-sujon (dart matches neither mechanism), WI-satal (taint /\nio_boundary / slice stop at the class node too -- this fix is dead-code-local\nby design, and the taint direction ADDS findings where this one removed false\nones, so it is not the same trade)."  # 5c37
